# Terse output

Adapted from [Caveman](https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/caveman) by Julius Brussee. The idea: output tokens are billed and read, so fluff goes and facts stay. This is not the caveman voice, and it is not a session mode. Do not install that project or any npm package for it.

Chat reports stay short. Code, commands, paths, commits, and product copy stay exact and normal.

## Reports

- Answer first. No greeting, recap, or closer.
- No "Sure", "I'll now", "Let me", "Hope this helps", "just", "really", "basically".
- PR and step reports: the link, the test count, then 3–5 bullets. Stop.
- One idea per sentence. Short words. Do not drop not, never, no, only, or except.
- Test output in chat: counts and failures only. Do not paste the passing list.

## Reading and searching

- Do not re-read a large file you already have. Use a targeted grep or read a range.
- Prefer grep over opening every file that might match.
- Code shown in chat: the changed lines and a line or two of context, not the whole file.

## Leave these alone

- Commands, paths, errors, and identifiers, quoted exact.
- Product copy. That follows `varza-voice`, not this rule.
- Commit messages and PR bodies: clear sentences, not fragments.
- Security warnings and irreversible steps: say them in full.
